  "limitations": [
    "SHA-256 minikey lengths 22 and 30, standard Base58 suffix, Bitcoin mainnet P2PKH/HASH160 only",
    "Legacy -m paths retain CPU behavior; length 26, PBKDF2, custom alphabets and random traversal are outside this slice",
    "No minikey throughput, multi-device scaling, calibration, tuning, partition or MIG certification claim",
    "Coordinator acceptance uses isolated localhost mTLS on each host; no public deployment"
  ],
  "findings": [
    "One-based fixed-width Base58 ordinals cover every candidate including invalid check bytes",
    "Internal mode-6 receipt scalar fields are ordinal coordinates; public result fields separate ordinal, text and derived scalar",
    "Direct scalar derivation is necessary because adjacent candidate hashes are unrelated; no point-stepping or power cache applies",
    "Canonical length/encoding/HASH160 targets preserve identity through recovery and authenticated file exchange",
    "Minikey jobs require an explicit sixth capability before allocation, renewal, updates or cached replay",
    "Two fixture variable collisions were corrected; the original CPU failure and successful offline rerun are retained",
    "Out-of-domain minikey creation is explicitly HTTP 400 before persistence, covered by final focused checks",
    "Supervisor leaves an unspecified kernel to mode defaults and rejects explicit stepped minikey execution"
  ],
  "evidence_policy": "Phased acceptance: source commits identify algorithm, storage, worker, example and final API-boundary content. The focused final boundary checks are separate from the earlier integrated worker gates. Embedded hashes identify each algorithm artifact, separately from final worker binaries. CPU offline fixture correction is recorded as a rerun, not hidden as an initial pass. Archive excludes credential contents and databases."
}
